      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 1856745
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-28T02:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "what may be confusing is that the log_show function matches the iteration pattern. It does not hold an inner loop but is called after each next.\nthe next and start functions are the one checking the end conditions.\nso we cannot force change the initial get pointer in the show functions.\nsee trusty_dump_logs on line 406.\nthe start function is given the initial offset which is set to last_successful_next in case of a panic.\nThis being said the way I did it in the trusty_dump_logs with the retry argument is not on-par with what we had because the retry will happen only once the linux kernel panics. I just fixed.\nDoes that make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "912e1851_565360ab",
      "revId": "1390f05d367ec1e5360690d66cd368bb0f708528",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "37a51e30_dac0bc84",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-28T02:11:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see that you started at last_successful_next when linux panics, but if trusty panics first, you would overwrite that before we got to that call. You have narrowed the problem in PS18, but there is still a race where trusty could panic after you set the start position but before call trusty_get_panic_status here.",
      "parentUuid": "c7460888_6bc1709d",
      "revId": "1390f05d367ec1e5360690d66cd368bb0f708528",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5fe30c9_75119893",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 157,
      "author": {
        "id": 1856745
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-29T16:08:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in the current implementation (the one mainlined), we check trusty_panicked only once and that is used to both start from the last successful get and disable rate limit gating. So in the mainlined implementation, if trusty panics while we\u0027re dumping the logs, we won\u0027t catch it until the start of the next log dump.\n\nIn this seq_file PS18 based implementation, we have this one time check (at the start of iteration) to decide whether to start from the last successful get. But then for each iteration we check trusty panic flag, this is indeed where there is a difference with the previous implementation.\nAnd if the trusty panic flag can change while we\u0027re dumping, this PS18 impl. breaks the retry feature.\n\n(*) But is it actually possible to have trusty panic flag updated while within the dump loop since we are in spin_lock_irqsave?\n\nAnyways PS19 fixes this potential issue by storing the trusty panic state at the start of the iteration.\n\nLooking forward to your answer to (*)",
      "parentUuid": "37a51e30_dac0bc84",
      "revId": "1390f05d367ec1e5360690d66cd368bb0f708528",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
